:: S5DRAIN: the x86 S5 PORT drains, so the DIRECT route drains too — ring filled to 64 line(s) / 4288 B (22x DRAIN_BYTE_BUDGET=192), one `acpi_power::s5_ring_flush()` — the symbol `poweroff()`'s first statement calls, which `video/crystal.rs` Shut Down and `video/instgui.rs` reach WITHOUT `power.rs` — put every line on the wire (lines=64 bytes=4288) and left the ring EMPTY (residue=0), 0 dropped; same `power_drain` entry point and same `[pwrshutoff]` family as `power.rs`, so there is ONE drain policy -> PASS ::
